  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAF_KIP Energy Efficiency strategy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to accelerate the phase-down of HFC and increase Energy Efficiency in South Africa&apos;s refrigeration and air-conditioning service sector and contribute to a reduction in greenhouse gas emissions. By addressing the slow decline in HCFC consumption in the service sector and the challenges associated with HFC alternatives, this initiative aligns with the HPMP Stage II Strategy, the Kigali Implementation Plan (in preparation), and national energy efficiency objectives. The project seeks to identify barriers to alternative refrigerant adoption, quantify potential energy efficiency improvements, develop guidance on suitable technologies, and enhance local capacity for environmentally friendly alternatives.</narrative>
  </description>
